            "caption": "Agentic AI is an emerging field of AI focused on building systems that can autonomously reason, plan, and execute complex tasks. These systems are made up of agents, which are typically large language models (LLMs), iterating through reasoning, calling tools, planning, reflecting, and using persistent memory to solve challenging problems over multiple steps. In the core of the agent, these areas are common: - ReAct Loop - Tool Calling - Planning & Decomposition - Reflection & Self-Critique - Structured Outputs For context and memory, the below areas are relevant: - Context compaction - Agentic RAG - Memory persistence - Prompt Caching Agents are able to use tools and orchestrate processes: - Tool Sandboxing - MCP Servers - Computer Use - Multi-Agent Systems - Routing and Handoffs - Workflow Graphs For reliability: - Guardrails & Verification - Agent Evals - Human in the loop - Tracing and observability - Cost and latency control These techniques are the core research foci for agentic AI, and ensure agents are reliable, safe, and scalable. It's no surprise agents are rapidly automating many everyday tasks and are used to tackle real-world problems. Learn AI, simply. Join 10000+ Others in our Visual AI Newsletter. Get your weekly research breakdown (link in bio 🔗). #machinelearning #deeplearning #math #coding #datascience",
