            "author": "future.with.ai98",
            "region": "TH",
            "shares": 457,
            "caption": "Google just released an AI agent setup that teaches itself to get better at every job 🤯 It's called Harness², and it's free and open source. Most AI agents do every task the same way forever, even when it isn't working. Harness² tries different approaches on the job and keeps whatever works best. Then it saves those lessons to a library, so the next job starts smarter. In Google's tests, agents scored up to about 11 points higher without changing the AI model. Search harness2 on GitHub. If you want to learn AI automation for free, link in the bio #Harness2 #GoogleResearch #AIAgents #OpenSource #AIAutomation #AI",
